#{[17592186543554 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543554 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105467" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543554 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543554 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $1$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=4t$ and $g(t)=3t-3$ with respect to the inner product." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543554 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb47ff23-1630-5500-b6a4-5200379ffde8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543554 #edb/ref 1074 "The distance between $f(t)=4t$ and $g(t)=3t-3$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-g(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖4t-(3t-3)‖ \\\\  & =‖t+3‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨t+3,t+3⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨t+3,t+3⟩ & =(t+3){|}_{0}\\cdot (t+3){|}_{0}+(t+3){|}_{1}\\cdot (t+3){|}_{1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{25}=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543611 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186543641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543611 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "25ebdf79-afa5-5b0e-8ef3-42e59a98265f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543611 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186543554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543620 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186543611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543620 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "32c4db97-0f9a-5a4a-9397-f3afd25d9b5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543620 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543641 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186543648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543641 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "71427223-2fdd-5bbd-81e0-02928d1f72bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543641 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186241063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543644 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 1759218